<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1500 0 R
/T (When an athlete has a submission hold in place in the outlying safety area, the referee should not interrupt the match.)
/E (When an athlete has a submission hold in place in the outlying safety area, the referee should not interrupt the match.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1501 0 R
/T (When an athlete has a submission hold in place and the opponent defends by moving to outside the outlying safety area, the referee should stop the match and restart it at the center of the match area with the athletes standing. In this case, when the referee deems it clearly apparent the athlete under attack initiated the movement that led to exiting the match area, he/she shall signal for two \(2\) points to be added to the score of the athlete performing the submission hold, as described in item 3.1.1.)
/E (When an athlete has a submission hold in place and the opponent defends by moving to outside the outlying safety area, the referee should stop the match and restart it at the center of the match area with the athletes standing. In this case, when the referee deems it clearly apparent the athlete under attack initiated the movement that led to exiting the match area, he/she shall signal for two \(2\) points to be added to the score of the athlete performing the submission hold, as described in item 3.1.1.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1502 0 R
/T (When one athlete takes his opponent to the outlying safety area while trying to stabilize a scoring position, the referee shall wait, whenever possible, for the athlete to stabilize the position for three \(3\) seconds before stopping the fight. If this happens, the referee will award the points and then restart the fight in the center of the combat area.)
/E (When one athlete takes his opponent to the outlying safety area while trying to stabilize a scoring position, the referee shall wait, whenever possible, for the athlete to stabilize the position for three \(3\) seconds before stopping the fight. If this happens, the referee will award the points and then restart the fight in the center of the combat area.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1503 0 R
/T (Points or advantages will be assessed for counting up until the safety area, and any movements performed outside the safety area will not be eligible for counting.)
/E (Points or advantages will be assessed for counting up until the safety area, and any movements performed outside the safety area will not be eligible for counting.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1504 0 R
/T (When the fight exits the combat area due to the movement of an athlete attacking a submission in hold, the referee will not mark two points after stopping the fight. Instead, the referee may give an advantage depending on the proximity of the submission, while respecting the rules of advantages \(Article 5th\).)
/E (When the fight exits the combat area due to the movement of an athlete attacking a submission in hold, the referee will not mark two points after stopping the fight. Instead, the referee may give an advantage depending on the proximity of the submission, while respecting the rules of advantages \(Article 5th\).)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
