/T (5.10  Doping Control Services: Tanzania Sports Alliance has the right to conduct doping control services in conjunction with its events, including sample collection and analysis, results management, and adjudication of disputes involving potential anti-doping rule violations. Compliance: It is the duty of competitors with their institutions to comply with all anti-doping rules of the World Anti-Doping Code and the Tanzania National Anti-Doping Committee, including Protocol for Olympic and Paralympic Movement Testing and all other policies and rules adopted by Tanzania Sports Alliance an Tanzania National Anti-Doping Committee. Arbitration and Testing: First instance arbitral decisions are final and not subject to appeal to the Court of Arbitration for Sport or any other body. Athletes agree to submit to drug testing by the Tanzania Sports Alliance an Tanzania National Anti-Doping Committee, or their designees at any time and understand that the use of methods or substances prohibited by applicable anti-doping rules makes them subject to penalties, including disqualification and suspension. Doping Violation Procedures: If it is determined that a member may have committed a doping violation, the member agrees to submit to the results management authority and processes of Tanzania Sports Alliance an Tanzania National Anti-Doping Committee.)
/E (5.10  Doping Control Services: Tanzania Sports Alliance has the right to conduct doping control services in conjunction with its events, including sample collection and analysis, results management, and adjudication of disputes involving potential anti-doping rule violations. Compliance: It is the duty of competitors with their institutions to comply with all anti-doping rules of the World Anti-Doping Code and the Tanzania National Anti-Doping Committee, including Protocol for Olympic and Paralympic Movement Testing and all other policies and rules adopted by Tanzania Sports Alliance an Tanzania National Anti-Doping Committee. Arbitration and Testing: First instance arbitral decisions are final and not subject to appeal to the Court of Arbitration for Sport or any other body. Athletes agree to submit to drug testing by the Tanzania Sports Alliance an Tanzania National Anti-Doping Committee, or their designees at any time and understand that the use of methods or substances prohibited by applicable anti-doping rules makes them subject to penalties, including disqualification and suspension. Doping Violation Procedures: If it is determined that a member may have committed a doping violation, the member agrees to submit to the results management authority and processes of Tanzania Sports Alliance an Tanzania National Anti-Doping Committee.)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
